Package: ros-lockdown
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: polkitd, pkexec, ros-agent (= @VERSION@)
Maintainer: ROS Project <yvesm189@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/yvesm189/ros
Description: ROS software installation policy
 Makes Isoko, the ROS Store, the only way software is installed on a
 workstation: PackageKit, apt and Flatpak's own authorisations are refused for
 anyone who is not an administrator, while the store needs no password at all.
 .
 The model is the one a phone uses - install freely, but only from a catalogue
 the organisation curates. Trust sits in the curation rather than in the user,
 and the agent behind the store accepts a catalogue slug rather than a package
 name, so installing from the store cannot become installing anything.
 .
 Also provides ros-run, which executes commands the management console has
 explicitly approved and nothing else.
